{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"ECS","modules":[{"name":"ECS"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"ECS"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them in a declared order."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted"],"anchor":"Essentials"},{"title":"Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule"],"anchor":"Modules"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ECS is an entity component system for Swift. It suits any program that updates many similar","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"things each step, such as the bodies of a physics simulation or the characters of a game.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entities are lightweight handles. An ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","isActive":true},{"text":" holds no data of its own.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Components are plain value types, such as a position or a velocity, attached to entities."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" holds the entities and their components, along with "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"resources","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values the world holds once, such as a clock."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems are rules that read and change the world through queries and updates, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs them in the order you write, at the same time where they don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conflict."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" runs a world frame by frame, with a fixed timestep and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"states.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A world is a copy-on-write value, like an array: copies are cheap and independent, so you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep one for a snapshot, an undo step or a rollback.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example, using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" components from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", spawns a ball and moves it one step by its velocity:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import ECS","","var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"import ECS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation, and you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"import one on its own.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ecs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Simulation"}],"title":"Simulation","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Simulation"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A world and its schedules by label, advanced one frame at a time."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule"},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS":{"title":"ECS","url":"\/documentation\/ecs","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them in a declared order."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS/GettingStarted":{"role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Define components, spawn entities, and move them with systems that run in a schedule and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simulation."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started with ECS","url":"\/documentation\/ecs\/gettingstarted"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"title":"Systems","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","title":"SimulationModule","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"title":"WorldModule","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Store the state of a game or simulation as entities and components, and read and change it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queries, updates, and commands.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Entity":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Entity"}],"title":"Entity","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/entity","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Entity"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldMod